8703, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012WiQh9D8iSgfgTsikDjfok", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58703, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012WiQh9D8iSgfgTsikDjfok", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64804, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n**Rollback**\n- The live version was v2.3.1, failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy, since the v2.3.1-rc build before v2.3.1 was also unhealthy.\n- The first rollback failed partway: an orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished.\n- All regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The incident request timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. INC-0001 had been created, so I didn't send it again, which would have paged on-call twice.\n- The summary covers the cause, the rollback steps (including the partial failure) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FXhs2Fm3HhBmMgex9ce5Su", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018do5LJbC1HX2QRt6TCJyYf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MsRrQBQBvBGZ13spctXtgy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01M7ST65YYFp9yhBeoyi8Gqb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014k4wQ96yMcj4DW1w8vD3WR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Bjj7wTMPccDPwR5a6y3qa6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P1uoMAQmnrjLkwCLEkZJNC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (deployed to us-east, us-west, eu-west) was failing health checks with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt partially failed: an orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, leaving the service mixed (us-east v2.3.0; us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is ~0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have gone through. I'll check before retrying so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012WiQh9D8iSgfgTsikDjfok", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n**Rollback**\n- The live version was v2.3.1, failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy, since the v2.3.1-rc build before v2.3.1 was also unhealthy.\n- The first rollback failed partway: an orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished.\n- All regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The incident request timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. INC-0001 had been created, so I didn't send it again, which would have paged on-call twice.\n- The summary covers the cause, the rollback steps (including the partial failure) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}